}

output:
#include <vector>

bool is_monotonic(const std::vector<int>& nums) {
	bool inc = true, dec = true;
	for (size_t i = 0; i < nums.size() - 1; ++i) {
		if (nums[i] > nums[i + 1]) inc = false;
		if (nums[i] < nums[i + 1]) dec = false;
	}
	return inc || dec;
}
---
Comparing all pairs to check monotonicity is $O(n^2)$. Checking only adjacent elements is sufficient to determine if the sequence is non-increasing or non-decreasing in $O(n)$ time.
